1
00:00:00,210 --> 00:00:01,600
Chapter two. Days away.

2
00:00:02,260 --> 00:00:03,680
The ceasefire mostly held.

3
00:00:04,250 --> 00:00:10,701
But talks in Islamabad failed, and on April thirteenth, a US naval blockade of Iran's ports took effect.

4
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:15,541
On April twenty-first, the ceasefire was extended, with no end date.

5
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:20,262
In May, the US struck Iran twice more, and called it self-defense.

6
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:23,002
And the deal was always almost done.

7
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:26,102
May twenty-third. Details "will be announced shortly."

8
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:29,463
June first. An agreement, "over the next week."

9
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:33,023
June ninth. Signing "could be in two or three days."

10
00:00:33,770 --> 00:00:39,480
Bitcoin didn't wait for it. From May thirty-first to June second, it fell more than nine percent.

11
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:42,844
By June thirtieth, it was at fifty-eight thousand five hundred.

12
00:00:43,450 --> 00:00:49,544
June seventeenth. Finally, a signed paper. The Islamabad Memorandum, with sixty days to negotiate.

13
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:53,805
The next day, the US ended the blockade, and Hormuz reopened.

14
00:00:54,330 --> 00:00:57,345
By early July, oil had slid below seventy dollars.

15
00:00:58,020 --> 00:00:59,765
For three weeks, it looked over.
